coder › Implemented `SlidingWindow` in `src/window.ts` and added tests in `src/window.test.ts`.

What changed
- Constructor now throws `RangeError` when `limit < 1` or `windowMs < 1`.
- Each key keeps its own array of event timestamps in a private `Map<string, number[]>`.
- `allow(key)` uses a single `now()` reading, prunes events at or before `now - windowMs` (so an event exactly `windowMs` old no longer counts), records only if the pruned count is below `limit`, and returns `false` without recording otherwise.
- `remaining(key)` returns `limit` minus the number of in-window events, pruning as it goes and deleting the key when it empties.

